__unwind_info laid out as Xcode 27.0's ld lays it out (B-193, docs/formats/build.md "Objective-C references,
archive members and hints in the linked image"): common encodings are those used by more than one entry, by
descending frequency then ascending encoding; the index reserves one entry per 511 entries and two more; each
second-level page starts where the previous one ends, rounded up to 8 bytes; the sentinel is one byte past the last
function. lld made every encoding common, ordered ties descending, gave each page 4096 bytes and put the sentinel at
the end.
